  <title id="bdl22imdbensembles-title">Accuracy of three ensembling strategies on IMDb and the optimized PAC-Bayes weighting</title>
  <desc id="bdl22imdbensembles-desc">Left panel: test accuracy against the number of independent training trials, from 2 to 30. The PAC-Bayes ensemble of all checkpoints rises from about 0.867 to about 0.875 and is the highest curve throughout; the uniform ensemble of the best checkpoints rises from about 0.863 to about 0.874, slightly below it; the uniform ensemble of all checkpoints stays much lower, rising from about 0.853 to about 0.861. Right panel: the optimized weights rho over 30 ensemble members (3 trials of 10 checkpoints). The first two checkpoints of each trial carry most of the weight, members 1, 2, 11, 12, 21 and 22 having weights between about 0.07 and 0.17, while the other members have weights below about 0.035. Members 1, 11 and 21, the checkpoints chosen by validation error, are drawn in a lighter fill.</desc>
